{title: How Can I Keep from Singing?}
{artist: Robert Lowry}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 88}

Verse 1
[D]My life flows on in [G]endless song;
Above earth’s lamentation
I [Am]hear the sweet though far [C]off hymn
That hails a new [G]creation:
Through all the tumult [D]and the strife
I hear the [Bm]music ringing;
It finds an [G]echo in my soul—
How [D]can I keep from singing?

Verse 2
What [G]though my joys and comforts [Am]die?
The Lord my Savior liveth;
[C]What though the darkness gather [G]round!
Songs in the night He [D7]giveth:
No storm can shake [G]my inmost calm
While to [D]that refuge clinging;
Since Christ is [Bm]Lord of Heav’n and earth,
[G]How can I keep from singing?

Verse 3
[D]I lift mine eyes; the [G]cloud grows thin;
I see the [D]blue above it;
And day [G]by day this pathway smoothes
[C]Since first I learned to love [G]it:
The peace of Christ [D]makes fresh my heart,
A fountain [G]ever springing:
All things are [D7]mine since I am His—
How [G]can I keep from singing?
